==Overview==
{{Frameless|[[File:OoT Navi Model.png|100px|right|thumb|Navi, a Fairy from {{OoT|-}}]]}}
Fairies usually have one of two roles in the series. Most Fairies possess healing powers; they can restore some of [[Link]]'s [[Heart]]s when he is wounded. From {{ALttP}} onwards, these Fairies can usually be caught in [[Empty Bottle]]s for later use. If Link falls in battle while carrying a bottled Fairy, it will automatically come out to revive him. Groups of Fairies can be commonly found in [[Fairy Fountain]]s scattered through the land, although some may also occasionally be found by breaking [[Pot]]s or cutting grass. In some games such as {{ALttP|-}}, [[Bubble]]s and [[Spark]]s can be turned into Fairies by using [[Magic Powder]] or the [[Boomerang]]. In {{SS}}, Fairies can be summoned by drawing the [[Triforce]] on a [[Goddess Wall]]. In {{BotW}} and {{TotK}}, Link is able to pick them up and store them despite the lack of Empty Bottles, though he needs to [[Stealth|sneak]] up on them to avoid detection.

The second role held by Fairies is that of a traveling companion. In several games, beginning with {{OoT}}, Link has been accompanied on his travels by Fairy companions. Although in many cases they are used to facilitate gameplay (allowing [[Targeting System|Z-Targeting]], for example), they also provide advice on what to do next or how to defeat certain enemies. In other games, such as {{PH}}, companion Fairies also serve as the cursor for guiding Link.

==={{TLoZ|-}}===
{{Stub|TLoZ}}
{{Descriptions TLoZ}}
Fairies occasionally appear after [[Enemy|Enemies]] have been defeated. Fairies fly around the screen until they make contact with [[Link]], fully healing him upon doing so. Fairies are depicted in the game's manual as blonde-haired humanoids with red dresses. However, both their clothes and hair are depicted as red in-game due to palette limitations.

==={{TAoL|-}}===
{{Stub|TAoL}}
Fairies sometimes appear when [[Monster]]s have been defeated. They will fully heal Link upon making contact with him. Link is also able to [[Transformation|Transform]] into a Fairy using the Spell of the same name. Doing so allows him to fly past [[Enemy|Enemies]] and through [[Locked Door]]s.

==={{ALttP|-}}===
{{Stub|ALttP}}
Fairies are depicted as pink-haired humanoids in blue dresses that congregate within [[Fairy Fountain]]s throughout [[Hyrule]]. In addition to appearing from slain [[Enemy|Enemies]], Fairies can emerge from bushes, [[Pot]]s, and [[Rock]]s. Link can capture Fairies in [[Empty Bottle]]s by using a [[Bug Net]]. Once captured, a Fairy will revive Link if he runs out of health, acting as an extra life. The Fairy then disappears, requiring him to either capture another one or have other bottled Fairies on hand to repeat the process. Link can also release the Fairy back into the overworld{{Verify}}<!-- Just the overworld? May be a misuse of terms -->, allowing him to either recapture it or consume it to heal a large chunk of his health.{{How Many}}

==={{LA|-}}===
{{Stub|LANS}}
In {{LA}}, Fairies are small creatures that [[Link]] can use to refill his [[Life Gauge]].{{How Many|LANS}} They appear when [[Mini-Boss]]es and certain [[Enemies in Link's Awakening|Enemies]] are defeated. They can also be found by [[Lifting]] certain [[Pot]]s,{{Which|LANS}} and within [[Great Fairy Fountain]]s.

With the addition of [[Fairy Bottle]]s in {{LANS}}, Link can catch Fairies and later release them at any time to [[Heal]] himself.{{How Many|LANS}} However, unlike [[Tracy]]'s [[Secret Medicine]], a Bottled Fairy will not revive him if all his [[Heart]]s are depleted.

