==={{OoT|-}}===
In {{OoT}}, every [[Kokiri]], with the exception of Link before [[Navi]] is assigned as his partner by the [[Great Deku Tree]], is partnered with such a guardian Fairy.<ref>{{Cite|The children of the forest, the Kokiri, live here with me. Each Kokiri has his or her own guardian fairy. However, there is one boy who does not have a fairy...|Deku Tree|OoT}}</ref> Fairies that are not partnered with a Kokiri appear throughout [[Hyrule]], restoring Link's health if he comes into contact with them. He can capture them in [[Bottle]]s to automatically restore his health if he falls in battle, or to manually restore his health by releasing them.

[[Butterfly|Butterflies]] can turn into Fairies if they land on the tip of a [[Deku Stick]].

Fairies are sold as [[Bottled Fairy|Bottled Fairies]] at the [[Medicine Shop]] for 50 [[Rupee]]s.

Another variety of Fairy called [[Big Fairy|Big Fairies]] resemble wingless, glowing balls. In certain areas, Link can play the [[Ocarina]] to make a Big Fairy appear.

==={{MM|-}}===
[[File:MM3D Stray Fairy Artwork.png|right|55px]]
{{Main|Stray Fairy}}
In {{MM}}, the [[Skull Kid]] had Fairy companions in [[Tatl]] and [[Tael]]. Tatl gets separated from them, and travels with Link to get his Hylian form back and to stop the [[Moon]] from crashing. [[Stray Fairy|Stray Fairies]] are the shattered portions of [[Great Fairy|Great Fairies]] that can be found throughout the [[Temple]]s and in [[Clock Town]].

Other Fairies in Termina can help restore Link's health if he comes in contact with them. Link can also capture them in [[Bottle]]s to receive their aid later. If he falls in battle, they will automatically escape from their Bottles and revive Link.

==={{OoS|-}}===
{{Stub|OoS}}
Fairies are commonly found in [[Pot]]s, inside tufts of [[Grass]], and sometimes from opening [[Gasha Nut]]s. Upon making contact with [[Link]], they restore six [[Heart]]s. They cannot be captured to revive Link on death, as this role is filled by the [[Magic Potion]].

==={{OoA|-}}===
{{Stub|OoA}}
Fairies can be found by breaking [[Pot]]s and by cutting [[Grass]]. Additionally, they can also be found inside [[Gasha Nut]]s. They will restore six [[Heart]]s on contact. Fairies cannot be captured to revive Link on death, as this role is filled by the [[Magic Potion]].

Three [[Stray Fairy|Forest Fairies]] are located in the [[Fairies' Woods]] in the present. These Fairies do not heal Link and instead challenge him to a game of hide-and-seek.

